WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:02.029
(light music)

00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:04.079
- I guess there's a certain part of me

00:00:04.079 --> 00:00:08.996
that's always thought that
computer parts look like cities.

00:00:10.415 --> 00:00:12.122
My name is Zayd Menk.

00:00:12.122 --> 00:00:15.945
I'm an 18-year-old
artist from Zimbabwe.

00:00:15.945 --> 00:00:18.528
(bright music)

00:00:21.001 --> 00:00:24.243
I grew up in a family of nine people.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:29.991
My parents had a repurposing
attitude towards most things.

00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:33.627
How can we use the rubbish
to make something else?

00:00:34.119 --> 00:00:38.872
So, I just make my artwork
out of the things that I find

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.080
and the things that I collect.

00:00:42.446 --> 00:00:46.862
I grew up in Harare, the
capital city of Zimbabwe,

00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:49.112
and I really like it there.

00:00:49.112 --> 00:00:51.150
But we do have quite a few challenges,

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:55.128
like political unrest
and economic challenges.

00:00:55.128 --> 00:00:58.023
There's also e-waste dumping
that has affected many

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:01.023
of the poorer areas around the city.

00:01:03.005 --> 00:01:04.850
This project that I'm working on

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.174
is a collaboration with HPE

00:01:08.174 --> 00:01:11.325
to make an area of Westminster

00:01:11.325 --> 00:01:14.225
done in recycled electronics.

00:01:15.922 --> 00:01:18.376
I think what I'm doing on a small scale

00:01:18.376 --> 00:01:21.851
is basically what they
doing on a large scale

00:01:21.851 --> 00:01:24.184
in a slightly different way.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:29.243
The parts for this project
were from HPE's facility.

00:01:30.793 --> 00:01:32.026
It was quite different,

00:01:32.026 --> 00:01:35.508
compared to what happened
for my first project.

00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:39.726
With that one, I had to go
around asking friends and family

00:01:39.726 --> 00:01:43.843
and trying to scavenge things
from the side of the road.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.713
When planning for this project,

00:01:46.713 --> 00:01:50.436
I used a lot of online
resources to calculate

00:01:50.436 --> 00:01:52.852
what area I'm going to do.

00:01:53.252 --> 00:01:57.358
It was also quite helpful
to see things in person.

00:01:57.358 --> 00:02:00.574
It puts things in
perspective quite nicely.

00:02:02.393 --> 00:02:06.148
From there I sketch out
the layout of the city,

00:02:06.148 --> 00:02:09.268
and I just start building
the individual buildings

00:02:09.268 --> 00:02:10.185
one by one.

00:02:11.565 --> 00:02:13.177
I think, in a perfect world,

00:02:13.177 --> 00:02:15.780
there wouldn't be such a thing as waste.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.009
Everything would be reused

00:02:18.009 --> 00:02:20.467
and repurposed for something else.

00:02:22.974 --> 00:02:26.087
- There are about fifty million
tons of e-waste generated

00:02:26.087 --> 00:02:27.422
on an annual basis.

00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:30.322
And substances that go into the products

00:02:30.322 --> 00:02:33.671
have impacts to soil, water, human health.

00:02:33.671 --> 00:02:37.052
We can't just take, make, dispose anymore.

00:02:37.052 --> 00:02:40.167
We need to really think
about how we responsibly

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:44.402
design, manufacture, and
dispose of the products,

00:02:44.402 --> 00:02:48.069
or potentially reuse them
at their end of life.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.960
The circular economy is a shift from

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.850
the traditional linear economy.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:56.316
Into a model where it's
regenerative in nature.

00:02:56.699 --> 00:02:58.448
One of the most exciting aspects

00:02:58.448 --> 00:02:59.836
of our environmental program

00:02:59.836 --> 00:03:02.567
are our technology renewal centers.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.071
Of the material that comes in the door,

00:03:04.071 --> 00:03:06.444
over 89 percent
is actually refurbished,

00:03:06.444 --> 00:03:09.324
remarketed and sold to new customers.

00:03:09.324 --> 00:03:12.955
The remaining portion is
recycled in a responsible way

00:03:12.955 --> 00:03:15.372
to have real impact at scale.

00:03:19.846 --> 00:03:22.961
- In the future, if
companies embrace the idea

00:03:22.961 --> 00:03:27.889
of the circular economy,
e-waste might not be an issue.

00:03:27.889 --> 00:03:32.465
And my artwork might be
seen as a sort of weird,

00:03:32.465 --> 00:03:34.986
historical artifact from a time

00:03:34.986 --> 00:03:37.806
when we didn't know any better.

00:03:37.806 --> 00:03:40.389
(mellow music)

